## Parity mapping (web -> native)
web/src/components/ai/AIFeedbackQueueTriage.tsx:
  • withAiFeature('feedback-queue-triage', InnerSection)  → AI-off gate; disabled ⇒ render nothing
       → native FeedbackTriageAvailability.resolved(enabled:false) ⇒ .gated phase (EmptyView)
  • useAiStream({ url: '/ai/feedback/triage/draft', body, onEvent })
       → FeedbackTriageRequest.path = "/ai/feedback/triage/draft"  (id in BODY, static URL)
  • haveFeedback = typeof feedbackId === 'number' && Number.isFinite(feedbackId) && feedbackId > 0
       → FeedbackTriageRequest.haveFeedback = feedbackID != nil && feedbackID > 0
         (Int is always finite; only the > 0 bound applies. 0 / negative are NOT valid selections —
          UNLIKE the vehicle-id surfaces where 0 passes. Locked by tests.)
  • body = haveFeedback ? { feedback_id: feedbackId } : { feedback_id: 0 }
       → FeedbackTriageRequest.body = ["feedback_id": haveFeedback ? feedbackID : 0]  (snake_case)
  • canStart = haveFeedback
       → FeedbackTriageProjection: canStart = FeedbackTriageRequest(feedbackID:).haveFeedback
  • AIFeatureCard title/description/buttonLabel/badge + AiOutputPanel
       → FeedbackTriageReady + FeedbackTriageOutputPanel (empty/thinking/prose/failed branches)
  • PROPOSE-ONLY: web references useUpdateFeedback ONLY in its header comments to state that this
    advisor NEVER calls the feedback mutation — the operator's manual triage controls remain the sole
    write path. The native surface preserves that contract: it binds the stream + i18n and never
    mutates feedback (no useUpdateFeedback peer wired — that would be a parity fabrication).
States reproduced: gated · loading · error(gate) · ready  ×  output {empty / no-feedback / thinking /
      prose / stream-error / unknown-error}  ×  freshness {live / stale / offline} (chip + banner +
      one-shot stale auto-refresh). a11y: VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type via tokens, Reduce Motion.
      P1/S11 view.opened telemetry deferred past the gate (web data-ai-feature marker parity).

